  "summary": "Claire Lomas, known for completing a marathon in a bionic suit after becoming paralysed, has died at age 44 due to an accident in Jordan. Previously, she had been injured in 2007, leading her to raise nearly £1m for charity. Notably, she completed the 2012 London Marathon in a bionic suit over 17 days and lit the Paralympic cauldron in Trafalgar Square. She also participated in the 2016 Great North Run while pregnant."
